# SEP-001

## The Poetics of Appetite:
A Practice-Based Investigation of Language in an Ice Cream Menu

Author: Jaiden Hordosillo

Published through:
Liminal Window
Studies in Everyday Poetics

ISSN: 3071-1932

Contents

- Research Paper (PDF)
- OpenTimestamps Verification (.ots)
- Verification Record (.txt)

Abstract

This study examines the linguistic strategies employed within a successful commercial ice cream menu and investigates the extent to which poetic mechanisms contribute to perceptions of desirability, appetite, and consumer engagement.
